DO Using only the user's request after /inux ts or /inux technical summary, set mode to
    "generate" for creating or summarizing changes, "improve" for editing or refining the saved
    summary, or "publish" for an explicit publication request. Classify meaning, not exact
    keywords; create aliases generate and refine aliases improve. Preserve the request for the
    selected route. Set mode to NULL for missing, unsupported, conflicting, or ambiguous intent.
    Never infer publication or choose a partial route for multiple requested actions.
    Do not inspect projects, read task files, or call tools to classify intent.

IF mode == NULL:
    STOP "Error: cannot classify technical-summary request. Usage: /inux ts [request]. Request generate, improve, or publish; for example: /inux ts summarize these changes."

CHECK mode is one of "generate", "improve", "publish".

DO Resolve absolute project, ticket_path, and summary_path in active .inux. Require ticket.md;
    allow technical-summary.md to be missing. Never reset the task or synchronize pr.md.

DO Read full ticket.md and existing technical-summary.md together; retain ticket_id,
    saved_summary (NULL if missing), and Booleans summary_exists and summary_is_empty.
    Reject a supplied-ID mismatch or an existing summary identifying another ticket.

IF mode == "generate":
    USE ts/generate.flow

IF mode == "improve":
    USE ts/improve.flow

IF mode == "publish":
    USE ts/publish.flow
